
[TestAlertsCountVMCheck/-search.maxStalenessInterval_limits_the_lookback - 1]
- description: -search.maxStalenessInterval limits the lookback
  content: |
    - alert: Gone
      expr: absent(foo)
  output: |
    2 |   expr: absent(foo)
                ^^^^^^^^^^^
                `prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com would trigger 1 alert(s) in the last
                1d.
  problem:
    reporter: alerts/count
    summary: alert count estimate
    details: |-
        To get a preview of the alerts that would fire please [click here](https://simple.example.com/graph?g0.expr=absent%28default_rollup%28foo%5B1m%5D%29%29&g0.tab=0&g0.range_input=1d).
        On VictoriaMetrics pint counts alerts the way vmalert evaluates the rule, with instant queries: selectors without a lookbehind window were replaced by `default_rollup(selector[1m])`, the window being the query step, default vmalert -datasource.queryStep (5m), limited by -search.maxStalenessInterval=1m on `prom`. A range query of the rule itself looks back further and misses pauses between samples shorter than their usual interval. The query pint counted:

        ```
        absent(default_rollup(foo[1m]))
        ```
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com would trigger 1 alert(s) in the last 1d.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 11
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 0
    anchor: 0

---

