[TestAlertsCountVMCheck/selectors_without_a_window_get_the_lookback_of_vmalert_instant_queries - 1]
- description: selectors without a window get the lookback of vmalert instant queries
  content: |
    - alert: Gone
      expr: absent(foo{job="bar"} offset 1h) and sum(rate(foo[5m])) > 0
  output: |
    2 |   expr: absent(foo{job="bar"} offset 1h) and sum(rate(foo[5m])) > 0
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                `prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com would trigger 1 alert(s) in the last
                1d.
  problem:
    reporter: alerts/count
    summary: alert count estimate
    details: |-
        To get a preview of the alerts that would fire please [click here](https://simple.example.com/graph?g0.expr=absent%28default_rollup%28foo%7Bjob%3D%22bar%22%7D%5B5m%5D+offset+1h%29%29+and+sum%28rate%28foo%5B5m%5D%29%29+%3E+0&g0.tab=0&g0.range_input=1d).
        On VictoriaMetrics pint counts alerts the way vmalert evaluates the rule, with instant queries: selectors without a lookbehind window were replaced by `default_rollup(selector[5m])`, the window being the query step, default vmalert -datasource.queryStep (5m). A range query of the rule itself looks back further and misses pauses between samples shorter than their usual interval. The query pint counted:

        ```
        absent(default_rollup(foo{job="bar"}[5m] offset 1h)) and sum(rate(foo[5m])) > 0
        ```
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com would trigger 1 alert(s) in the last 1d.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 59
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 0
    anchor: 0

