[TestAlertsCountVMCheck/step_from_group_params - 1]
- description: step from group params
  content: |
    - name: g
      params:
        step: ["30s"]
      rules:
      - alert: Gone
        expr: absent(foo) or bar > 0
  output: |
    6 |     expr: absent(foo) or bar > 0
                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                  `prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com would trigger 1 alert(s) in the
                  last 1d.
  problem:
    reporter: alerts/count
    summary: alert count estimate
    details: |-
        To get a preview of the alerts that would fire please [click here](https://simple.example.com/graph?g0.expr=absent%28default_rollup%28foo%5B30s%5D%29%29+or+default_rollup%28bar%5B30s%5D%29+%3E+0&g0.tab=0&g0.range_input=1d).
        On VictoriaMetrics pint counts alerts the way vmalert evaluates the rule, with instant queries: selectors without a lookbehind window were replaced by `default_rollup(selector[30s])`, the window being the query step from `params` of its group (30s). A range query of the rule itself looks back further and misses pauses between samples shorter than their usual interval. The query pint counted:

        ```
        absent(default_rollup(foo[30s])) or default_rollup(bar[30s]) > 0
        ```
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com would trigger 1 alert(s) in the last 1d.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 22
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 6
        last: 6
    severity: 0
    anchor: 0

